 Raspberry Pi
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a section for running the whole dashboard against the bundled mock
printer and camera, so the interface can be evaluated before buying anything.
Verified end to end: npm run check passes against the mocks and the app serves
the real dashboard.

Also records the two genuine alternatives to a Pi, with their limits stated
rather than implied: Octo4a on a spare Android phone (real OctoPrint, but
charging and USB OTG conflict on some handsets), and the MKS WiFi module the
SV02's Robin Nano board accepts (wireless file transfer only — it replaces the
SD card, not the computer, so it cannot provide the camera, alerts or this
app).
